      detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer:**\n\nUNION combines result sets and removes duplicate rows. UNION ALL combines result sets without removing duplicates. Because duplicate elimination requires additional work such as sorting or hashing, UNION ALL is usually faster when duplicates are valid or impossible by design. Both queries must have compatible numbers and types of columns in corresponding positions.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```sql\nSELECT email FROM customers\nUNION\nSELECT email FROM leads;\n```\n\nUNION removes duplicate emails. UNION ALL keeps every occurrence.",
