      detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer:**\n\nThe optimizer chooses the access path it estimates will have the lowest cost. It may prefer a table scan when a predicate matches a large percentage of rows, when an index is poorly selective, when statistics are inaccurate, or when the query applies an expression/function that prevents efficient index use. Data type mismatches, leading wildcards, implicit conversions, and unsuitable composite-index order can also contribute. Use EXPLAIN and current statistics rather than assuming the index must be used.\n\n**Example:**\n\nWHERE LOWER(email) = 'a@x.com' may not use a normal index on email efficiently.\n\nA suitable generated/functional indexing strategy, where supported, can address the expression.",
